WLAN
5.4.6.1 The Contractor must utilise a computerised Trouble Ticketing System to track and provide details of each incident reported by TSPOC to include, at a minimum, the following information:
a) Ticket number;
b) Date of the ticket;
c) Name of the person reporting the incident;
d) Client Department name and location of the incident;
e) Name of the person receiving the monthly incident report;
f) Description of the incident (minor, major or critical);
g) Severity of the incident;
h) Description of the incident resolution; and
i) Time to restore.
DLAN
(166) The Incident Tickets must include, but not be limited to, and the Contractor must maintain, the following dedicated information fields for all Incidents:
a) Ticket number;
b) Incident description;
c) Incident originator (Contractor, Canada representative);
d) related Incident Tickets;
e) related Change Tickets;
f) date and time stamp when Incident initiated;
g) date and time stamp when Incident closed;
h) Incident type (production, functional testing, performance testing, security, etc.) as
specified by Canada;
i) Incident severity;
j) Incident status (i.e., open, closed, in progress, suspended, cancelled, etc.);
k) Canada’s ticket number;
l) Service function impacted;
m) Service Desk contact to initiate ticket (name, telephone number and email address);
n) Contractor’s contact information (name, telephone number and email address);
o) Client Organization/User identifier (as specified by Canada);
p) Client Organization/User type (as specified by Canada);
q) Client Organization/User language;
r) Department’s contact information (name, telephone number and email address);
s) activity log including all actions taken by third parties;
t) resolution description and cause;
u) outage time (for closed tickets only); and
v) date and time stamp when ticket last updated.
